<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Daumantas of Pskov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1299">1299</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Dovmont, Timothy of Pskov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Daumantas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pskov">Pskov</a> was a Lithuanian prince who took part in the murder of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindaugas">Mindaugas</a> in 1263 and then fled to Pskov. Baptised as Timothy, he ruled Pskov as its prince from 1266 until his death in 1299 and defended it against the Livonian Order. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-orthodox-church">Russian Orthodox Church</a> venerates him as a saint, and part of the Pskov kremlin bears his name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/daumantas-of-pskov.jpg" alt="Daumantas of Pskov" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: shakko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mirozhskaya.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
